Atlas overlay patch 0097: ui/sidebar-foot
Why: in the reel (scene 3, pose atlas-ntp-light) the "New tab" row with its shortcut is the foot of
the sidebar, under its rule, whatever the number of tabs; the engine's bottom container grows with
the free space but keeps its button at the top, so with a few tabs the row followed the last tab.
Aligning the container's content to its end puts the row at the foot (and the + of the collapsed
rail at the bottom of the rail). No setting places it, so this is two alignment lines.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/vertical/vertical_tab_strip_bottom_container.cc
Test filter: *AtlasSidebar*; reel-check scene R02 (footer row at the foot of the sidebar)
Rebase risk: L (two lines in one small function)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in a file the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/vertical/vertical_tab_strip_bottom_container.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/vertical/vertical_tab_strip_bottom_container.cc
@@ -86,8 +86,13 @@
 
   // Setting button's layout based on collapsed state
   SetOrientation(orientation);
+  // Atlas (patch 0097): the "New tab" row is the foot of the sidebar, under a
+  // rule, however few tabs there are (reel scene 3); the space above it stays
+  // free (window caption).
   SetCrossAxisAlignment(collapsed ? views::LayoutAlignment::kStretch
-                                  : views::LayoutAlignment::kStart);
+                                  : views::LayoutAlignment::kEnd);
+  SetMainAxisAlignment(collapsed ? views::LayoutAlignment::kEnd
